    "body": "## Summary\n\n- bind completion request, completion confirmation, and direct cancellation locks to the authorized worker/requester before lifecycle state is read\n- make instant acceptance lock only `OPEN + INSTANT` jobs; preserve the public `OPEN + PROPOSALS` conflict without loading terminal/private rows through the global lock\n- return the same neutral not-found response for missing and out-of-scope lifecycle resources so mutation endpoints cannot be used as existence/status oracles\n- add regression tests proving outsider requests stop before the legacy global lock, persistence, escrow release/refund, and tracking cleanup\n- document the lifecycle authorization, concurrency, and financial-ordering boundary\n\n## Risk / invariants\n\n- authorized actors still receive lifecycle conflicts after the actor-scoped pessimistic lock succeeds\n- completion settlement ordering and direct-cancellation refund ordering are unchanged\n- no schema or migration changes\n- public `OPEN` assignment-mode semantics are preserved\n\n## Validation\n\nThis PR must pass the repository's exact-head CI/runtime, CodeQL, container-security, payments-ledger and platform-fee gates before merge.",
